\1\n    <div id="site-header"></div>
    <!-- Header -->
    
    <main class="lesson-container py-4">
        <!-- Breadcrumb -->
        <div id="tutorial-header"></div>
        
        <div class="content lesson-content" style="font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text-secondary);">
            <p>DNS (Domain Name System) is the phonebook of the internet. It translates human-readable domain names (like <code>google.com</code>) into IP addresses (like <code>142.250.190.46</code>) that computers use to connect to each other.</p><h3>Troubleshooting Tip</h3><p>If you can access websites by their IP address but not by their name, you have a DNS issue. Try changing your DNS server to <code>8.8.8.8</code>.</p><h3>Related Command</h3><p>Use <a href='../../commands.html' class='cmd-badge' style='display:inline-block'>nslookup</a> to troubleshoot DNS resolution.</p>
        </div>
        
        <!-- Navigation -->
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color); padding-top: 1.5rem; margin-top: 3rem;">
